  "limits": [
    "Native start BLOCKED: serve_windows_scm_service loads a trusted v2 T037 profile before ServiceMain. No AppContainer profile, SID, project/session ID or trusted profile is materialized by this unit; no fake GUID/SID or loader bypass.",
    "Service-state and child writable leaf ACLs are deliberately not granted. Real startup needs a separately scoped actual profile/provider/resource and explicit writable-leaf setup.",
    "SYSTEM owner creation requires an already capable context: SYSTEM or an elevated admin token with SeRestorePrivilege already enabled. This module does not enable/acquire that privilege or spawn another bootstrap process. Main must select any real authorized initial context.",
    "Input is not the current b90 offline preview package as-is. Normal CPython offline pip materialization and the approved complete inventory must be provided separately; this unit does not claim the package apply_ready.",
    "Original-owner restore is in-process only. Loss of original handles/journal after process death is not permission for name-only adoption or automatic replay; no durable cross-process restore capability is claimed.",
    "SCM comparison covers the exact queried base config, SID type, RequiredPrivileges, failure actions/flag, status, raw object SD and dependents; no all-registry/all-host/DLL closure proof is claimed.",
    "Full AppContainer/WFP apply/restore remains in existing modules. Existing AppContainer RESTORE_NOT_IMPLEMENTED remains an independent gap.",
    "T037 causal isolation, admission, native enforcement and the overall universal goal are not accepted by these software tests."
  ],
